'''''Gladiolus carneus''''' is a plant species in the family [[Iridaceae]].<ref>{{cite web|title=''Gladiolus carneus'' F.Delaroche | work=The Plant List|url=http://www.theplantlist.org/tpl1.1/record/kew-328305|accessdate=12 October 2015}}</ref>
[[File:Gladiolus carneus.jpg|thumb|''Gladiolus carneus'']]
[[File:Gladiolus carneus Kleinmond Oct 2013 (2).jpg|thumb|''Gladiolus carneus'']]
Common name for this plant is Painted Lady Gladiolus. A tunicated corm, it is summer dormant. Native to South Africa in a dry summer - wet winter climate. Grows about 50&nbsp;cm high. Very ornamental and a good cut flower.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://asa.co.il/varieties-all/gladiolus-carneus/|title=Gladiolus carneus - Asa Flowers Bulbs|work=Asa Flowers Bulbs|access-date=2018-11-11|language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.pacificbulbsociety.org/pbswiki/index.php/Gladiolus_carneus|title=Pacific Bulb Society {{!}} Gladiolus carneus|website=www.pacificbulbsociety.org|access-date=2018-11-11}}</ref>

==Cultivation==
''Gladiolus carneus'' grows well in the ground in Mediterranean climates or anywhere in pots. It reliably comes back. Can be dug and stored for the summer. Keep it dry in the summer. Plant in autumn with 5&nbsp;cm (2&nbsp;in) of soil over the bulb and 5 – 10&nbsp;cm (2 - 4 inches) apart.

